# Pinned OpenSSL engine (ADR-001). Sourced by scripts/build-openssl.sh, the
# release workflow, and asserted by tests/engine.
#
# Update policy (ADR-007): check
# https://openssl-library.org/news/vulnerabilities/ regularly and before each
# release. If the pinned version is affected, bumping it here is top priority.
#
# 3.5.x is the LTS branch (EOL 2030-04-08) and is the first release with native
# ML-KEM / ML-DSA / SLH-DSA in the default provider.
#
# 3.5.7 (2026-06-09) is the latest *released* 3.5.x patch and the first without
# a known unpatched High-severity issue: 3.5.6 and earlier are affected by
# CVE-2026-45447 (heap use-after-free in PKCS7_verify).
#
# Known open against 3.5.7 as of 2026-08-19: CVE-2026-14456 (Low, announced
# 2026-08-13) — unbounded memory growth in the QUIC *server* incoming-channel
# queue. Upstream names 3.5.8 as the fix, but 3.5.8 has not been released yet,
# so there is nothing to bump to. It also cannot affect this project: we drive
# the engine as a `genpkey`/`req`/`x509`/`verify` subprocess and never run a
# QUIC server, and `serve` (F4) will use `s_server` over TLS, not QUIC.
# openssl-watch.yml opens an issue the week 3.5.8 appears.
OPENSSL_VERSION=3.5.7
OPENSSL_SHA256=a8c0d28a529ca480f9f36cf5792e2cd21984552a3c8e4aa11a24aa31aeac98e8
